# Webhook target uses HTTPS
# Platform: GitHub (SDLC::Webhook assets)
# CTN: github_webhook
# Frameworks: KSI-CNA-RNT, KSI-SVC-SNT, NIST SC-8, SC-8(1), CMMC SC.L2-3.13.8

META
    esp_id `github-webhook-uses-https-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `github`
    criticality `high`

    category `asset_list`
    target_asset_type `SDLC::Webhook`

    title `Webhook target URL uses HTTPS`
    description `Validates that the repository webhook POSTs to an https:// URL. Plaintext http:// webhooks leak payload contents (commit metadata, pushed file diffs, author email, branch names) to anyone on-path between GitHub and the receiver.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `github,sdlc,webhook,tls,transport,ksi-cna-rnt,ksi-svc-snt,nist-sc-8,cmmc-sc-l2-3.13.8`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CNA-RNT,KSI:KSI-SVC-SNT,NIST-800-53:SC-8,NIST-800-53:SC-8(1),CMMC:SC.L2-3.13.8`
    control_objective `KSI-CNA-RNT,KSI-SVC-SNT,SC.L2-3.13.8`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`
    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `GitHub:scanset:sdlc-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Repo Settings, Webhooks, edit the offending webhook: change "Payload URL" from http:// to https://. If the receiver does not support TLS, replace it with one that does; do not relax the policy.`

    component_id `comp-github-sdlc`

    impl_KSI_CNA_RNT `Runtime network traffic from the SDLC platform to downstream consumers is required to traverse TLS. The webhook payload URL is the egress channel; mandating https:// ensures the payload (commit refs, author identifiers, repo state) is confidentiality-protected in transit. The CTN reads the live config.url field and the policy fails when the scheme is not https.`
    impl_KSI_SVC_SNT `Service network traffic confidentiality is enforced at the application layer by mandating TLS on webhook receivers. This complements network-layer controls (egress firewalls, TLS-only L7 LBs) and prevents misconfiguration at the application layer from silently downgrading.`
    impl_SC_L2_3_13_8 `Confidentiality of CUI-adjacent metadata in transit (commit author email, branch contents) is preserved by requiring TLS on all webhook deliveries. The policy detects http:// targets and emits a finding for each.`

META_END

DEF
    # Default placeholder values, overridden per-asset by PolicySetSync
    # at bind time. PolicySetSync rewrites the SET body with one OBJECT
    # per bound webhook (one webhook == one SDLC::Webhook asset).
    VAR owner string `_unbound_`
    VAR repo string `_unbound_`
    VAR webhook_id int 0

    # Bound assets - managed programmatically by PolicySetSync from
    # inventory.asset_policies (status = active). Do not hand-edit;
    # the SET body is the only mutable region of this file.
    SET github_webhooks union
        OBJECT webhook_target
            owner VAR owner
            repo VAR repo
            webhook_id VAR webhook_id
        OBJECT_END
    SET_END

    STATE webhook_is_https
        found boolean = true
        uses_https boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN github_webhook
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF webhook_is_https
            SET_REF github_webhooks
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
